Celephin the Elf (my first character in 14 months to get so far!) 
just reached the Sanctum of Moloch today.  He found the secret door,
was challenged by the high priest, whereupon a black dragon behind
Celephin decided to breathe and disintegrate the priest.  He left 
a corpse, but nothing else:  in particular, no Amulet.  The Wizard
showed up again shortly afterward, but he didn't have it, either,
when Celephin killed him.  WHAT DO I DO?  This is my best game
ever, and my wife (who ascends with awe-inspiring ease) assures me
that it should be somewhere on the level, and that I've explored all
of it.  Is this a bug?  Did the Wizard perchance steal it when I wasn't
looking and take it back to his tower?  Please help me!  


(Incidentally, the other spoiler isn't related, but is something
I discovered when trying to get myself out of another really unpleasant
situation.  Hit 'n' (or, better yet, 'r'---tell me how to solve my problem)
now if you don't want to see it.




















I was taking a troll corpse out of Fort Ludios to drop it in the moat,
and forgot that I wasn't wearing my ring of levitation---sunk like a rock,
was too burdened to climb out, and dropped random stuff (including 
Grayswandir and my BoH!).  Since I hadn't seen an amulet of magical
breathing, and the bag was much too heavy to kick out (thank Erevan
that Grayswandir was on top!), I thought that I was screwed at least until
I could find a wand of polymorph to polypile my useless amulets (and a
lot of other useless stuff).   Then, in the course of scouring the
dungeon in an attempt to find one of the necessary objects, I came
across a wand of teleportation, and had a strange idea.

Yes, it worked:  if you happen to know where some valuable underwater
stuff is, levitate over it and zap a wand of teleportation straight
down ('>').  The pile will be randomly scattered all over the level,
which on the Medusa or Juiblex levels would be a real pain, but in
this case it was a godsend.

I recall that the question of recovering stuff from under water 
was addressed on r.g.h. a while ago, but I don't remember this
solution being posted, so I felt obliged to post it (by the way,
a wand of teleportation also can be used to recover items stuck in
undiggable walls).

I will be very grateful for any solutions to my main problem,
either sent by private e-mail or posted to rec.games.hack.

Thanks to everyone in advance.

